WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.150
For dedicated TV fans, getting attached to
your favorite characters is part of the fun

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.340
of watching — but things can get ugly when
one of them gets bumped off.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.720
Whether they're objecting to the concept of
passing in general or to a particular brutal

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.830
and undeserved end, fans aren't shy about
letting everyone know how mad they are when

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.780
their fave kicks the bucket.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:17.860
"How DARE you!"

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:21.300
Here's a look back at some of the character
deaths that have upset fans the most over

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:25.240
the years — and here's your chance to click
away if you don't want to see any spoilers.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:30.040
"Stop it, stop it both of you, you're spoiling
it, you're spoiling everything!"

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:31.700
Lexa, The 100

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.880
This post-apocalyptic CW drama spurred outrage
when it bumped off Lexa, played by Alycia

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.780
Debnam-Carey.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:41.860
Not only was Lexa a fan favorite, but her
development arc had just reached an important

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.660
milestone: she and her romantic interest Clarke,
played by Eliza Taylor, had just slept together

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.400
for the first time.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:51.440
Fans were angry about the interrupted storyline,
but also incensed by the way Lexa's death

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.420
seemed to imply that the show saw its gay
characters as "disposable."

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:59.270
The backlash was so intense that showrunner
Jason Rothenberg ultimately apologized to

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:01.660
fans — but there was no undoing the source
of their heartbreak.

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:08.280
"Sex and death came so close together and
I'm aware of the optics of that being uncomfortable."

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:09.860
Wash, Firefly

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:15.200
Joss Whedon's series about outer-space cowboys
had legions of dedicated fans who were left

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.970
hanging when the show was cancelled after
just one season — a problem Whedon tried

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:21.240
to resolve with a follow-up feature film,
Serenity.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:25.499
But while fans were thrilled to get some closure,
they weren't happy at all with this moment

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.860
in the movie's third act, when Wash, played
by Alan Tudyk, is killed by harpoon-wielding

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:30.360
Reavers.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.720
"I'm a leaf on the wind….

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.260
Watch out..."

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:41.090
Despite being devastated, most Firefly fans
processed their grief and anger and eventually

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:41.980
found some peace.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.060
But others couldn't let go; one man even claimed
that Wash's death defied the laws of physics,

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:48.440
just like Mal's beloved ship.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.940
"Love keeps her in the air when she oughta
fall down."

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.720
Adriana, The Sopranos

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:57.180
In a mobster series that's filled with gruesome
murders, none was more tragic than the death

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:59.640
of Adriana La Cerva, played by Drea de Matteo.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.819
Adriana is a good person who just wants to
escape into Witness Protection with her boyfriend,

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:08.110
Christopher — but Christopher betrays her,
which she realizes at the same time the audience

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.980
does in her heart-wrenching final scene.

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.540
It was so brutal that some fans tried to find
hope in the fact that Adriana was off-camera

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.360
when Silvio pulled the trigger.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:19.240
Could it be that, like Tony Soprano, she's
not really dead?

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:20.660
"Don't stop!

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.260
Believin!

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.960
Hold on to that feeeeeeeeelin!"

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.500
Joyce Summers, Buffy the Vampire Slayer

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:34.140
After being ill for most of the fifth season,
Buffy's mother Joyce is finally starting to

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:34.640
get better.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.720
But then, Buffy returns home to find her mother
motionless on the couch — dead from a sudden

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:40.860
brain aneurysm.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:44.940
Many fans were deeply upset with showrunner
Joss Whedon for doing away with off Joyce — and

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.280
they weren't the only ones.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.820
Even Buffy herself, Sarah Michelle Gellar,
argued against the decision.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.420
"And I tried so hard to talk him out of it,
I was not happy about it."

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:57.330
Although most fans now agree that "The Body"
is one of the best episodes of the entire

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:01.740
series, processing Joyce's passing definitely
took some time, and a lot of tears.

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.480
Lane Pryce, Mad Men

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:08.150
Despite signs throughout season five of Mad
Men that Lane was struggling with some heavy

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:12.360
stuff, his self offing was still one of the most
upsetting moments in Sterling Cooper history.

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.360
The ad man played by Jared Harris had embezzled
$7,800 from the agency to cover a debt, a

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.260
crime that Don Draper discovers.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:24.070
In despair, Lane returns to the agency, types
a resignation letter, and hangs himself.

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.580
"I think there's something terribly wrong
in Mr. Pryce's office."

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:32.040
The distraught reactions of Lane's coworkers
mirror those of fans, who were devastated

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.100
to see their favorite character meet such
a tragic, untimely end.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.160
Derek Shepherd, Grey's Anatomy

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:42.280
The doctor known as "McDreamy" was central
to this Shonda-land drama — particularly

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.930
his rocky relationship with fellow doc Meredith
Grey.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:49.360
But just when the couple looked like they'd
live happily ever after, a car accident leaves

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.140
Derek brain-dead.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:54.960
Meredith has to make the difficult decision
to remove him from life support, a plot twist

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.840
that left many fans wanting to pull the plug
themselves... on their televisions.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:00.480
"Are you ready?

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:04.640
-No.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:06.680
But go ahead."

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:08.560
Colonel Blake, MASH

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.040
In this light-hearted comedy series, the sudden
and unexpected death of Lieutenant Colonel

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.220
Blake in the third season was unprecedented.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.520
When actor McLeanStevenson decided to leave
the series, the show's creators wrote Blake

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.900
off with an honorable discharge — only to
cap the episode with a devastating epilogue.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:32.080
"Henry Blake's plane was shot down over the
sea of Japan."

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.860
The show received over a thousand letters
from viewers who didn't appreciate this incredibly

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.240
depressing moment in a show that was supposed
to be funny.

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:42.460
And they weren't alone: the networks were
so upset about the scene, CBS even cut it

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.720
entirely in later airings of the episode.

00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:46.500
Jax Teller, Sons of Anarchy

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:52.180
In the 2014 series finale of Sons of Anarchy,
the anti-hero played by Charlie Hunnam made

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:57.620
a controversial exit from the show — and
the mortal plane — by fleeing from the police...right

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.780
into the path of an oncoming eighteen-wheeler.

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.500
Jax's end didn't sit well with fans; some
thought he deserved better, and others thought

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.680
he deserved worse, but above all, everyone
thought that the computer-generated crows

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.180
in the final shot looked completely ridiculous.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.200
Dan Conner, Roseanne

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:23.620
In the final season of the long-running sitcom
Roseanne, things take a turn for the weird.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:28.360
The Conner family wins the Illinois Lottery,
Roseanne goes on Jerry Springer, Dan has an

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.500
affair, and —

00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:34.280
"My writing is really what got me through
the last year after Dan died, I mean, at first

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.660
I felt so betrayed like he had left me for
another woman."

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:38.940
Wait, what?!

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:43.240
As it turns out, Dan is dead — taken by
a heart attack at Darlene's wedding — and

00:05:43.460 --> 00:05:47.200
the crazy fantasies of season nine were just
Roseanne's way of coping with her grief.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:52.140
Many fans and critics weren't too happy with
the bait-and-switch, but in this case, there's

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:56.240
good news: John Goodman's Dan will be back
from the dead in the Roseanne revival, which

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.900
is reportedly going to pretend that the show's
ninth season never even happened.

00:06:00.620 --> 00:06:02.240
The Red Wedding, Game of Thrones

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:07.140
While HBO's fantasy series is notorious for
doing away off its characters, this multiple

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.100
passing is the one fans just can't get over.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:14.080
After reconciling with the easily-offended
Lord Walder Frey, Robb Stark and his retinue

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.200
attend the marriage of Edmure Tully to Frey's
daughter, Roslin.

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.660
And everything seems to be going well!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.620
Until suddenly, it isn't.

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:24.820
"Rob!"

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:30.340
Within just a few minutes, Game of Thrones
gets rid of off Robb Stark, his wife Talisa, his

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:32.500
mother Catelyn, and his direwolf Grey Wind.

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:37.460
Twitter exploded with angry, profanity-laced
tirades about the killings, with fans blaming

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.180
Walder Frey, Roose Bolton, and the Lannisters
— but also the showrunners, George R.R.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:45.740
Martin, and any friends who had read the books
and didn't warn them ahead of time.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:46.980
The moral of this story?

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:48.880
Take it away, Ramsay Bolton:

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:55.160
"If you think this has a happy ending, you
haven't been paying attention."

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:56.500
Thanks for watching!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.920
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.400
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

